        "procedure": "Evaluate 735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1001(b) as an independent alternative for any personal property, even when subsection (a), (c), or (e) also applies. For EV, its whole-asset ceiling is $4,000 for one debtor and $8,000 for two joint debtors; claim no more than the asset value. Under subsection (c), a motor vehicle receives at most $2,400 for the whole named vehicle. Limit subsection (a) to necessary wearing apparel, bibles, school books, and family pictures; subsection (d) to actual tools or books of the debtor's trade; and subsection (e) to professionally prescribed health aids.",
        "avoid_when": "Do not use these personal-property exemptions for business-use property. Do not call jewelry wearing apparel or ordinary household property a tool of trade without the required facts, and do not double the subsection (c) vehicle ceiling merely because two debtors jointly own the vehicle."
      }
    ],
